1
00:00:09,739 --> 00:00:10,740
This means…

2
00:00:10,824 --> 00:00:12,450
To spice up their marriage,

3
00:00:12,534 --> 00:00:15,245
the wife dressed up and role-played
as different types of women.

4
00:00:15,328 --> 00:00:16,538
And were going on dates?

5
00:00:16,621 --> 00:00:18,289
It's a wonderful thing!

6
00:00:18,373 --> 00:00:20,166
That's right, it's lovely!

7
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:21,417
That is what true love is.

8
00:00:21,501 --> 00:00:23,127
<i>I want to get married too.</i>

9
00:00:23,211 --> 00:00:27,006
<i>We're on a hard-earned vacation,</i>
<i>so we've got to find some romance.</i>

10
00:00:27,090 --> 00:00:28,508
<i>Romance, huh.</i>

11
00:00:28,591 --> 00:00:31,094
<i>Midori, you seriously need</i>
<i>to get a boyfriend soon!</i>

12
00:00:31,177 --> 00:00:34,472
<i>Not having dated a guy at your age</i>
<i>is honestly a red flag!</i>

13
00:00:34,556 --> 00:00:37,684
Let’s invite some guys over
and have a mixer at this villa!

14
00:00:37,767 --> 00:00:38,935
A mixer at the villa…

15
00:00:39,018 --> 00:00:40,645
Sounds just like
a reality show, I love it.

16
00:00:40,728 --> 00:00:41,771
<i>A reality show?</i>

17
00:00:41,855 --> 00:00:43,106
<i>Like a dating show?</i>

18
00:00:44,232 --> 00:00:46,526
<i>I wonder if I'm even capable</i>
<i>of falling in love.</i>

19
00:01:17,056 --> 00:01:18,183
Mr. Nishigami!

20
00:01:19,601 --> 00:01:21,895
You picked summer oranges for us.

21
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:25,607
Leaving too many on the tree
puts a strain on it.

22
00:01:26,316 --> 00:01:27,317
I see.

23
00:01:30,695 --> 00:01:32,071
They smell so good, freshly picked!

24
00:01:32,655 --> 00:01:34,782
I'll make freshly squeezed juice!

25
00:01:34,866 --> 00:01:35,950
Right!

26
00:01:36,034 --> 00:01:38,953
If you add honey,
it gets sweet and super delicious!

27
00:01:39,829 --> 00:01:41,247
I bet you already knew that.

28
00:01:44,626 --> 00:01:45,960
Where are Konta and the others?

29
00:01:46,044 --> 00:01:49,172
My brother went grocery shopping,

30
00:01:49,923 --> 00:01:52,759
and Tetsuro is fishing, I think?

31
00:01:53,968 --> 00:01:55,595
So today is…

32
00:01:58,431 --> 00:02:00,516
Yes! It’s a girls' day.

33
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:02,602
I see.

34
00:02:03,394 --> 00:02:05,897
-Well then…
-Oh, wait…

35
00:02:09,442 --> 00:02:10,652
There he goes.

36
00:02:13,029 --> 00:02:16,282
Maybe I shouldn't have said
it was a girls' day.

37
00:02:19,994 --> 00:02:22,413
It's an orange. Oh, so cute!

38
00:02:22,497 --> 00:02:24,332
We really need to budget better.

39
00:02:24,415 --> 00:02:25,500
Looks good!

40
00:02:29,003 --> 00:02:31,089
Hello? Konta? What's up?

41
00:02:31,172 --> 00:02:33,841
I’m buying groceries.
Do you need anything?

42
00:02:33,925 --> 00:02:36,970
<i>Oh, perfect timing!</i>
<i>Just get whatever is cheap.</i>

43
00:02:37,053 --> 00:02:38,972
<i>We'll be staying</i>
<i>at this villa for a while,</i>

44
00:02:39,055 --> 00:02:41,307
<i>so we need to keep food expenses down.</i>

45
00:02:41,391 --> 00:02:42,558
Got it!

46
00:02:44,978 --> 00:02:47,146
Cheap stuff.

47
00:02:49,983 --> 00:02:52,276
Okay, this goes on Instagram.

48
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:53,444
What?

49
00:02:53,528 --> 00:02:54,487
What?

50
00:02:54,570 --> 00:02:55,613
Mikako…

51
00:02:56,197 --> 00:02:57,573
got married!

52
00:02:57,657 --> 00:02:58,616
What?

53
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:00,410
Mikako? Our classmate?

54
00:03:00,493 --> 00:03:01,285
Yes!

55
00:03:01,369 --> 00:03:02,996
-Oh, wow.
-What?

56
00:03:03,079 --> 00:03:04,080
Whoa!

57
00:03:04,163 --> 00:03:05,790
He looks so respectable.

58
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:11,087
Mikako totally got plastic surgery.
Doesn't her nose look smaller?

59
00:03:11,170 --> 00:03:13,506
She did nothing but go to mixers in Tokyo.

60
00:03:13,589 --> 00:03:15,174
Must have reeled in a good one.

61
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:18,386
Wait, hold on!

62
00:03:18,928 --> 00:03:21,305
Suzuki from the class next to ours
got married too!

63
00:03:21,389 --> 00:03:22,598
-Seriously?
-What?

64
00:03:22,682 --> 00:03:24,017
That plain girl?

65
00:03:30,565 --> 00:03:34,736
I wonder where everyone meets
their soulmates.

66
00:04:07,310 --> 00:04:10,104
Cheap stuff…

67
00:04:11,522 --> 00:04:13,983
Radishes? One hundred yen?

68
00:04:14,567 --> 00:04:17,862
R-Radish? What?

69
00:04:17,945 --> 00:04:18,988
These…

70
00:04:21,657 --> 00:04:23,910
These are turnips. Red turnips.

71
00:04:23,993 --> 00:04:27,121
Midori told me to get whatever is cheap.
This is definitely the cheapest.

72
00:04:27,205 --> 00:04:31,542
Radish, turnip, red turnip!

73
00:04:32,418 --> 00:04:33,586
Oh, Midori?

74
00:04:33,669 --> 00:04:35,171
I'm heading back soon.

75
00:04:35,254 --> 00:04:37,465
But listen, like, today,

76
00:04:37,548 --> 00:04:40,218
these tiny little turnips
were ridiculously cheap!

77
00:04:40,301 --> 00:04:42,053
Radi? Radi…

78
00:04:42,136 --> 00:04:44,555
Whatever, they're turnips!

79
00:04:44,639 --> 00:04:46,599
They were practically giving them away!

80
00:04:46,682 --> 00:04:48,351
So, I bought the entire stock!

81
00:04:48,434 --> 00:04:51,270
I bought every single turnip!
See ya later.

82
00:04:52,021 --> 00:04:53,064
What?

83
00:04:53,147 --> 00:04:54,357
She hung up already.

84
00:04:54,857 --> 00:04:56,275
-Man, Midori…
-Excuse me.

85
00:05:00,196 --> 00:05:03,574
I wonder what Mikako's husband
makes in a year.

86
00:05:03,658 --> 00:05:05,701
Maybe… like 20 million yen?

87
00:05:05,785 --> 00:05:06,953
What?

88
00:05:07,036 --> 00:05:09,288
-She doesn't have to worry about money.
-True.

89
00:05:09,372 --> 00:05:13,459
I want a rich, handsome husband too.

90
00:05:13,543 --> 00:05:14,585
Hey.

91
00:05:14,669 --> 00:05:16,963
The new season of <i>Last Princess</i>
is streaming!

92
00:05:17,046 --> 00:05:18,673
-What?
-You love it, right, Rinrin?

93
00:05:18,756 --> 00:05:20,216
All right, let’s watch it! Right now!

94
00:05:20,299 --> 00:05:23,469
I'm in the mood for romance,
so we are watching this now!

95
00:05:23,553 --> 00:05:24,679
Huh…

96
00:05:25,304 --> 00:05:27,765
I haven't really watched
this kind of stuff before.

97
00:05:33,604 --> 00:05:38,651
<i>On this season of</i> Last Princess<i>,</i>
<i>our leading man is…</i>

98
00:05:47,535 --> 00:05:49,120
I'm Kotaro Komiyama.

99
00:05:49,704 --> 00:05:53,124
I run multiple restaurants in Tokyo.

100
00:05:53,916 --> 00:05:56,836
<i>On this journey,</i>
<i>I hope to find my ultimate partner</i>

101
00:05:56,919 --> 00:05:58,671
and return to Tokyo together.

102
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:02,049
<i>Through my hobby,</i>

103
00:06:02,133 --> 00:06:04,552
<i>I've built up some muscles.</i>
<i>That's my charm.</i>

104
00:06:05,136 --> 00:06:09,140
<i>When your shoulders get broad like this,</i>
<i>it gives you a real sense of presence.</i>

105
00:06:09,223 --> 00:06:13,102
I feel like it helps elevate me
as a business owner,

106
00:06:13,186 --> 00:06:14,437
so I work hard at it.

107
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:15,354
<i>Yes.</i>

108
00:06:15,438 --> 00:06:17,398
This guy seems super shady.

109
00:06:17,481 --> 00:06:19,150
Total meathead vibes.

110
00:06:19,859 --> 00:06:21,736
<i>As for my type, let's see.</i>

111
00:06:21,819 --> 00:06:24,780
<i>Definitely someone who laughs a lot,</i>
<i>a cheerful girl.</i>

112
00:06:25,865 --> 00:06:29,160
<i>Right now, I'm extremely driven</i>
<i>when it comes to my work.</i>

113
00:06:29,243 --> 00:06:32,538
<i>I'm the type to act</i>
<i>the moment I get an idea.</i>

114
00:06:32,622 --> 00:06:34,123
<i>I don't like negative people.</i>

115
00:06:34,207 --> 00:06:39,503
<i>I prefer someone cheerful</i>
<i>who can take anything positively.</i>

116
00:06:40,755 --> 00:06:44,675
The woman who steals this guy's heart
gets to be the last princess!

117
00:06:44,759 --> 00:06:46,761
Oh, I see.

118
00:06:46,844 --> 00:06:49,430
They're looking
for someone to marry, after all!

119
00:06:49,513 --> 00:06:51,682
-Really?
-Everyone goes all out to seduce him.

120
00:06:51,766 --> 00:06:54,727
-So they actually get married?
-Sometimes they do.

121
00:06:54,810 --> 00:06:56,020
For real.

122
00:06:56,103 --> 00:06:57,688
I bet it's scripted.

123
00:06:57,772 --> 00:07:00,650
Midori! If you talk like that,
you can't enjoy dating shows!

124
00:07:00,733 --> 00:07:01,943
Oh, okay.

125
00:07:02,610 --> 00:07:04,820
Is she a female candidate?

126
00:07:23,297 --> 00:07:24,298
<i>I'm Airi.</i>

127
00:07:24,382 --> 00:07:28,177
I'm 27 years old. I work as a model.

128
00:07:28,886 --> 00:07:30,555
Wow, she's gorgeous!

129
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:33,808
She's totally a pro at this romance stuff.

130
00:07:34,433 --> 00:07:36,102
She's totally making it to the end.

131
00:07:36,185 --> 00:07:37,603
She's not all that.

132
00:07:37,687 --> 00:07:38,604
What?

133
00:07:38,688 --> 00:07:41,023
For a reality show these days,
she's on the weaker side.

134
00:07:41,107 --> 00:07:42,567
Seriously?

135
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:45,736
Nice to meet you.

136
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:47,196
Nice to meet you.

137
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:48,823
-I'm Airi.
-Airi.

138
00:07:48,906 --> 00:07:52,868
I came on this journey
to become your number one, Kotaro!

139
00:07:53,703 --> 00:07:54,870
I'm flattered.

140
00:07:54,954 --> 00:07:56,706
-Thank you.
-Cringe!

141
00:07:56,789 --> 00:07:58,499
"Number one" is a cringe line?

142
00:07:58,583 --> 00:08:02,545
This girl is just using this show as
a stepping stone to become a celebrity.

143
00:08:02,628 --> 00:08:05,506
She has zero intention
of marrying this guy.

144
00:08:05,590 --> 00:08:06,924
It’s clout chasing.

145
00:08:18,019 --> 00:08:19,061
Nice to meet you.

146
00:08:19,145 --> 00:08:20,313
Nice to meet you.

147
00:08:20,396 --> 00:08:21,689
I'm Kotaro Komiyama.

148
00:08:22,898 --> 00:08:24,650
Hooray, hooray,

149
00:08:24,734 --> 00:08:25,943
Kotaro!

150
00:08:26,777 --> 00:08:29,947
A Spirit Bomb that lights up
everyone's day! I'm Moka!

151
00:08:30,615 --> 00:08:31,866
Spirit Bomb?

152
00:08:31,949 --> 00:08:34,452
Apologize to Mr. Akira Toriyama right now!

153
00:08:35,411 --> 00:08:36,412
In my daily life,

154
00:08:36,495 --> 00:08:39,749
I'm a cheerleader for a basketball team
in Chiba Prefecture.

155
00:08:40,249 --> 00:08:42,043
<i>He's completely my type.</i>

156
00:08:42,126 --> 00:08:46,088
<i>He has such a great build</i>
<i>and he's handsome. Totally my type.</i>

157
00:08:46,172 --> 00:08:48,341
I really want to make him mine.

158
00:08:49,467 --> 00:08:51,636
Do you like short girls?

159
00:08:52,219 --> 00:08:54,597
I do like shorter girls, yes.

160
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:58,100
Watch, Moka is going to do
the hand-size comparison thing

161
00:08:58,184 --> 00:09:00,269
just to show off how tiny she is.

162
00:09:00,353 --> 00:09:02,104
Midori, pour some alcohol! Alcohol!

163
00:09:02,188 --> 00:09:03,939
What? You're drinking in the morning?

164
00:09:06,192 --> 00:09:07,735
Turn around for a second.

165
00:09:07,818 --> 00:09:09,737
-You want me to? Okay.
-Yes.

166
00:09:19,914 --> 00:09:22,416
Moka only comes up to here.

167
00:09:24,251 --> 00:09:25,711
You're so big.

168
00:09:27,129 --> 00:09:28,756
Right, yes.

169
00:09:28,839 --> 00:09:30,549
She exceeded my expectations.

170
00:09:30,633 --> 00:09:32,385
Moka is a serious tactician.

171
00:09:32,468 --> 00:09:34,512
Her power level is insane!

172
00:09:34,595 --> 00:09:38,641
<i>My heart skipped a beat.</i>
<i>The physical contact was unexpected.</i>

173
00:09:39,266 --> 00:09:41,352
She was incredibly cute.

174
00:09:52,321 --> 00:09:53,572
<i>I do that a lot.</i>

175
00:09:53,656 --> 00:09:56,325
It’s my best feature,

176
00:09:56,409 --> 00:09:58,828
so I made sure to use it
to its full potential.

177
00:09:58,911 --> 00:10:01,414
Girls like that always win.

178
00:10:02,123 --> 00:10:04,083
-I used to play basketball.
-Really?

179
00:10:04,166 --> 00:10:05,960
I also really love watching pro-wrestling.

180
00:10:06,043 --> 00:10:07,044
-I see.
-Yes.

181
00:10:07,128 --> 00:10:09,505
-And I go to saunas a lot too.
-Saunas too?

182
00:10:09,588 --> 00:10:10,756
-Yes.
-Do you like saunas?

183
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:11,924
-I love saunas.
-Wow!

184
00:10:12,007 --> 00:10:13,551
I actually really like saunas too.

185
00:10:13,634 --> 00:10:15,928
-Really? We should go together.
-Yes!

186
00:10:16,011 --> 00:10:18,180
-A sauna date sounds great. Yes!
-Let's do it.

187
00:10:18,264 --> 00:10:21,851
I also think about saunas
from a business perspective.

188
00:10:21,934 --> 00:10:25,271
I want to combine the restaurants
I run with a sauna concept.

189
00:10:25,354 --> 00:10:27,022
-Wow, you're amazing!
-Not really.

190
00:10:27,106 --> 00:10:28,858
Saunas are very trendy right now.

191
00:10:28,941 --> 00:10:31,026
They are, they're super popular.

192
00:10:31,110 --> 00:10:33,863
You're such a sharp businessman
to see opportunity in that!

193
00:10:34,405 --> 00:10:38,075
There it is!
Those are staple lines of popular girls.

194
00:10:38,159 --> 00:10:39,618
-"You're amazing!"
-"I didn't know that!"

195
00:10:39,702 --> 00:10:40,995
-"Wow!"
-"You have great sense!"

196
00:10:41,078 --> 00:10:42,288
"I see!"

197
00:10:42,371 --> 00:10:44,915
You two are amazing!

198
00:11:00,514 --> 00:11:01,515
Nice to meet you.

199
00:11:01,599 --> 00:11:02,683
Nice to meet you.

200
00:11:03,267 --> 00:11:04,935
-I'm Kotoko.
-Kotoko.

201
00:11:05,019 --> 00:11:06,187
Yes.

202
00:11:06,270 --> 00:11:10,357
Well, to be honest,
I quit my job to come meet you.

203
00:11:10,441 --> 00:11:11,275
What?

204
00:11:13,068 --> 00:11:15,070
-You quit your job?
-Yes, I did.

205
00:11:15,696 --> 00:11:18,699
<i>I worked at a food manufacturer</i>
<i>for five years.</i>

206
00:11:18,782 --> 00:11:22,495
Now, I've left the company,
so I am unemployed.

207
00:11:22,578 --> 00:11:24,788
Unemployed! Just like me!

208
00:11:25,831 --> 00:11:27,917
Wow, to have that level of commitment…

209
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:28,834
Yes.

210
00:11:29,460 --> 00:11:31,587
I'm flattered.

211
00:11:31,670 --> 00:11:33,631
-Yes.
-I'm glad.

212
00:11:33,714 --> 00:11:35,841
-I love bold people.
-Oh, really?

213
00:11:35,925 --> 00:11:37,927
-Yes. I'm thrilled.
-Thank you.

214
00:11:39,345 --> 00:11:40,930
-Actually…
-Yes?

215
00:11:41,013 --> 00:11:45,476
I heard that you are
very particular about your diet.

216
00:11:45,559 --> 00:11:47,144
-Yes.
-Well…

217
00:11:48,354 --> 00:11:49,605
What's that?

218
00:11:50,648 --> 00:11:53,067
I went and got certified
as a food advisor!

219
00:11:53,150 --> 00:11:54,735
Wait, a food advisor?

220
00:11:54,818 --> 00:11:55,861
-Yes!
-Really?

221
00:11:57,404 --> 00:11:58,989
-It's the real deal.
-Incredible!

222
00:11:59,573 --> 00:12:01,951
Oh, she has qualifications.

223
00:12:02,034 --> 00:12:03,160
So she's not like me.

224
00:12:03,744 --> 00:12:06,497
There are always girls like that
who collect certifications.

225
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:08,582
Don't worry, Midori.
You don't need any of that!

226
00:12:08,666 --> 00:12:10,292
You can make a cocktail this good!

227
00:12:10,376 --> 00:12:12,962
-That's your benchmark?
-Cheers!

228
00:12:13,045 --> 00:12:14,755
-Cheers.
-Yay.

229
00:12:26,392 --> 00:12:27,393
Nice to meet you.

230
00:12:27,476 --> 00:12:28,519
Nice to meet you.

231
00:12:29,270 --> 00:12:31,730
I came here to find
my very first boyfriend.

232
00:12:31,814 --> 00:12:34,316
I'm Mayumi, 25 years old,
from Ibaraki Prefecture.

233
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:36,360
It's a pleasure to meet you.

234
00:12:36,443 --> 00:12:39,238
Right now, I'm working part-time
while attending a training school

235
00:12:39,321 --> 00:12:40,781
to become a voice actress.

236
00:12:41,699 --> 00:12:44,326
Well, "first boyfriend" is a little heavy.

237
00:12:44,410 --> 00:12:45,536
What?

238
00:12:45,619 --> 00:12:46,704
Really?

239
00:12:46,787 --> 00:12:48,831
-I look forward to getting to know you.
-Likewise.

240
00:12:48,914 --> 00:12:51,792
That's wonderful. I absolutely love people
who chase their dreams.

241
00:12:51,875 --> 00:12:53,043
-Really?
-Yes.

242
00:12:53,127 --> 00:12:55,838
-I would like to join forces--
-Have you achieved your dreams?

243
00:12:55,921 --> 00:12:58,257
-No, not even close.
-Not yet?

244
00:12:58,340 --> 00:12:59,592
I'm only halfway.

245
00:12:59,675 --> 00:13:01,176
-Halfway?
-Yes!

246
00:13:01,677 --> 00:13:03,637
What kind of person is your type?

247
00:13:04,305 --> 00:13:08,934
Well, I like people who are like aliens.

248
00:13:09,852 --> 00:13:11,270
-Aliens?
-Yes.

249
00:13:11,353 --> 00:13:13,772
There it is, the quirky ditz persona.

250
00:13:13,856 --> 00:13:17,067
When you can't win with a conventional
approach, you have to act weird.

251
00:13:17,985 --> 00:13:19,987
Oh, aliens?

252
00:13:20,070 --> 00:13:21,071
That's cute.

253
00:13:22,698 --> 00:13:24,867
<i>I blurted out how cute she was.</i>

254
00:13:24,950 --> 00:13:28,704
She had an innocent,
carefree vibe, and I liked it.

255
00:13:29,288 --> 00:13:30,956
Wow, she struck a chord.

256
00:13:31,040 --> 00:13:34,543
Girls like her surprisingly
make it far in these shows.

257
00:13:37,796 --> 00:13:42,176
I want to do my best
and get them to open their hearts.

258
00:13:42,926 --> 00:13:45,471
I see. I look forward to it.

259
00:13:46,263 --> 00:13:48,974
Jeez, this guy is an idiot.

260
00:13:49,058 --> 00:13:50,768
Oh, speaking of which, Rinrin,

261
00:13:50,851 --> 00:13:54,063
didn't you apply
for<i> Last Princess </i>a few years back?

262
00:13:54,647 --> 00:13:56,857
Yes, a long time ago.

263
00:13:57,441 --> 00:14:01,111
To catch the judges' attention,
you tried to act ditzy, right?

264
00:14:01,195 --> 00:14:03,822
Yes. But they just thought
I was dumb and dropped me.

265
00:14:03,906 --> 00:14:05,449
What a dark past!

266
00:14:05,532 --> 00:14:08,369
But if it were now,
I would totally dominate this show!

267
00:14:08,452 --> 00:14:10,537
You do have plenty of dating experience.

268
00:14:10,621 --> 00:14:13,165
We’re staying
in this gorgeous villa, after all.

269
00:14:13,248 --> 00:14:16,293
I want to have a romance
like <i>Last Princess </i>too!

270
00:14:20,756 --> 00:14:22,007
Coming!

271
00:14:22,675 --> 00:14:24,385
Nice to meet you.

272
00:14:24,468 --> 00:14:26,387
Who are you?

273
00:14:26,971 --> 00:14:30,516
Mr. Konta invited us over!

274
00:14:31,433 --> 00:14:32,977
What?

275
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:34,311
Seriously?

276
00:14:34,395 --> 00:14:35,729
Isn't this just like…

277
00:14:35,813 --> 00:14:37,773
Our very own reality dating show?

278
00:14:37,856 --> 00:14:39,733
-I've got to put on makeup.
-What?

279
00:14:39,817 --> 00:14:42,069
-Me too!
-Huh? Wait… Well…

280
00:14:42,152 --> 00:14:43,153
Uh…

281
00:14:43,237 --> 00:14:45,155
Please wait just a moment.

282
00:15:06,093 --> 00:15:07,511
They smell so good, freshly picked!

283
00:15:40,377 --> 00:15:42,087
<i>We came here from Tokyo.</i>

284
00:15:42,171 --> 00:15:44,757
He said, "We're having a barbecue
at my villa, you should come."

285
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:46,967
They're handsome and successful!

286
00:15:47,051 --> 00:15:50,345
<i>-Perhaps they are…</i>
<i>-Our dating show has finally begun!</i>

287
00:15:51,805 --> 00:15:53,849
<i>I'm Midori, Konta's younger sister.</i>

288
00:15:53,932 --> 00:15:57,186
<i>When it comes to cooking and cleaning,</i>
<i>I work harder than anyone!</i>

289
00:15:57,269 --> 00:15:59,188
<i>I'm Rinrin, Midori's friend.</i>

290
00:15:59,772 --> 00:16:03,525
<i>I think it's about time</i>
<i>I find that one special soulmate.</i>

291
00:16:03,609 --> 00:16:05,194
<i>Likewise, I'm her friend, Tsumugi.</i>

292
00:16:05,277 --> 00:16:08,864
<i>I came here to experience</i>
<i>the passionate love of a lifetime.</i>

293
00:16:08,947 --> 00:16:10,783
<i>I don't plan on holding back.</i>

294
00:16:10,866 --> 00:16:12,076
<i>-I will…</i>
<i>-Definitely…</i>

295
00:16:12,159 --> 00:16:15,370
Find a good person
and go back to Tokyo with him!

296
00:16:15,454 --> 00:16:16,413
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

